[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"664","stub":{"id":"664","section":"Saylor to Hyden (up to 28 miles)","altname":"","river":"Kentucky, Middle Fork","difficulty":"ItoII","states":["USA-KEN"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"67","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"This is the more likely best put-in.\n\nDrainage area is now up to a more reasonable 20.9 square miles.\n\nFrom here to the listed access at Asher is around 7 miles, and could be the 'best' (and more often boatable) section of this branch of the river.\n\nGradient starts with just over a mile at  62 FPM, then drops to 37 FPM for the next mile, and 23-27 FPM the remaining miles.\n\nAgain, while we have no specific knowledge of this section of river, that first mile or two seems likely to contain decent whitewater (likely at least class II, possibly into class III, and could also involve major scouting and portaging). The remaining miles are likely swiftwater and class I-II.\n\nWe highly encourage anyone who has put eyes on this area to help out fellow boaters with a \"Trip Report\" (especially if you can provide photos!). Are there rapids worthy of naming? Mandatory portages? Major problems with wood?","id":"109274","location":{"latitude":"36.972044","longitude":"-83.449187"},"name":"Warbranch: Hwy.1850 at Middle Fork Road","distance":"5.97","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"Hyden River Front Park should provide wonderful parking and access.\n\nNOTE: this river (branch) description formerly listed a take-out at Buckhorn. The gradient from Hyden to Buckhorn is all very minimal. While that stretch is certainly paddleable, we are doubtful that it contains sufficient rapids to be included in this whitewater inventory. If you have experience with paddling it, and if it actually does have some whitewater merit, please add a Trip Report (with photos, if possible) to elaborate on that section.","id":"114513","location":{"latitude":"37.163144","longitude":"-83.372276"},"name":"Take Out: Hyden River Front Park","distance":"27.94","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"16639","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9498","description":"this is actually on rock bridge branch before swift camp creek. after about seven inches of rain.","caption":"The Decent Descent","poi_name":"Creation Falls","subject":"John","author":"Jake Keunzli","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/16639","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/16639"}}],"detail":{"id":"664","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"This listing is highly tentative, based upon sketchy reports which did not detail put-in or take-out locations. As a result,best put-in and take-out are unknown, and all of what is listed here is highly tentative. We have listed the highest likely/possible put-in to the point where gradient mostly peters out. In general, gradient is steepest early on, and mostly diminishes as the listed reach progresses.\n\nWhile a gauge (with drainage listed as 206 square miles) has been in place at Hyden since 2018, it only provides precipitation and gauge height data (no cfs conversion). In 2022, a gauge was added near Buckhorn (drainage area 421 square miles), but it appears to have just one reading per day. Thus, we remain linked to the gauge at Tallega (drainge area 537 square miles, in place since 1986). Using relative drainage areas, flow at Hyden _might_ be on the order of 0.3836 times the gauge at Tallega. (That gauge will lag considerably both on the rise and fall, but should be reasonable approximation when flows are relatively stable.)\n\n**Anyone with specific information and experience with any part of this run is encouraged to provide a trip report listing your put-in, take-out, gauge reading (either stage at Hyden, flow at Buckhorn, or ideally both), and evaluation of runnability and difficulty, and nature of rapids encountered.**\n\nSome detail may be available in the guidebook Canoeing & Kayaking Guide to KY","averageGradient":"14","maxGradient":null,"length":"28","correlations":[{"reachID":"664","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":"Likely under 200 cfs at Hayden. Likely too low for decent whitewater.","lowRunnableRangeComment":"Possibly 200-500 cfs at Hayden. Likely low-boatable.","mediumRunnableRangeComment":"Possibly 500-1000 cfs at Hayden. Likely moderate flows.","highRunnableRangeComment":"Possibly 1000-2000 cfs at Hayden. Likely high-boatable.","aboveRecommendedRangeComment":"Likely massive flows. (5200-10400 cfs >> Possibly 2000-4000 cfs at Hayden. *** 10400+ cfs >> Possibly 4000+cfs at Hayden.)","lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"520","beginMediumRunnable":"1300","beginHighRunnable":"2600","endHighRunnable":"5200"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"MIDDLE FORK KENTUCKY RIVER AT TALLEGA, KY","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"03281000","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"67","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"4.68","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"37.55508768","longitude":"-83.5937993"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/03281000","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/03281000/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"67","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["